                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Air Combat Arena is a game a friend sent my way to try out. Essentially, it's a dogfighter sim, although there is also a mini game mode where you fly around in a bi-plane collecting planets.\n\nFirst off: you WILL be playing against bots. There are zero active servers, which makes sense since today's peak amount of players was one (me) with four all time peak players. So, as far as things go, this isn't actually a bad dogfighter. The controls are a bit wonky, and inverted for some reason, which makes them even seem a bit looser, but all in all it controls well. This would be far more fun with friends I think however, as bot fights lost their charm quickly.\n\nThe little mini game I mentioned is very relaxing, with a looped chill EDM track playing.\n\nThe graphics are decent for what this game presents. The battle map is fairly bland, but I feel this works for the minimalist nature of the game. The mini game features some far more interesting and trippy visuals IMO.\n\nOutside of that EDM track, I can't think of anything else from an audio standpoint outside of the sounds of battle, which are much like the graphics.\n\nAlso, the achievements seem to be broken. I've definitely shot down planes while trying this game out.\n\nAll in all, I was skeptical of the mostly positive rating going in, and I'm honestly a bit on the fence here myself. On one hand, it is a decent game. On the other hand, it gets boring quickly without the inclusion of real multiplayer due to a lack of player base (which is odd since I know with the current bundle it's in, there are at least a few hundred if not thousands of owners. I'm giving it a flat 5/10 and a thumbs up for now, but there really isn't much here w/o said MP battles.\n\n[code]If you found this review helpful and would be interested in supporting my Curator group, it would be appreciated. Cheers.\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/curator/32549618/[/code]",
